From bd0584007d0670cbabd7da8a8e016803739913a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 05:55:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] fix(ops): a pinned host upgrades to the next release,
 not to the tip of main
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

install.sh now clones the newest release tag, which leaves the checkout on a
detached HEAD. upgrade.sh read that as the branch name "HEAD" and ran
`git pull --ff-only origin HEAD`, quietly fast-forwarding the host onto main
— the unpinned behaviour the pin exists to prevent (review B-24).

A detached checkout is now upgraded release to release: resolve the newest
vX.Y.Z on the remote, fetch that tag and check it out. A remote without
release tags warns and leaves the tree alone instead of pulling a branch.
scripts/tests/test-release-pin.sh covers both halves against real local
repositories — version ordering (v1.10.0 over v1.9.3, rc tags ignored), the
upgrade hop, the already-newest no-op, and the untagged remote.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UTnpHajSmkk2JMLfuQoV7o
